  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Swedish Tax Agency fact finding mission Georgia</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Swedish Tax Agency fact finding mission Georgia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Swedish Tax Agency (STA) will jointly with Georgian Revenue Service (GRS) work on a project proposal STA to support GRS</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Swedish Tax Agency (STA) will jointly with Georgian Revenue Service (GRS) work on a project proposal STA to support GRS</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Swedish Tax Agency (STA) approached Sida with a request to support (Service Purchase Agreement) a fact-finding mission in order to outline possible cooperation areas where STA can contribute to strengthening the Georgian Revenue Service (GRS) with a focus on capacity building.

The objectives of the fact-finding missions are:

1) To establish contact with key staff and management at the GRS and other relevant stakeholders such as the Embassy of Sweden, EU, IMF, World Bank and other donors of importance for designing the possible future support, and 2) To collect information from the GRS and the tax system in Georgia as well as the context where the authority is operating. Elaborating a strategic analysis of the current situation and needs is also envisaged.

Based on the achievements of the fact-finding mission, the overall objective will be to identify areas of possible Swedish support and to prepare a draft project document, including potential areas, objectives and modalities of a future cooperation betwen the two agencies.</narrative>
  </description>
